15 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting patient selection for a study on spinal infections from 2015 to 2023, showing enrollment, exclusion criteria, allocation to three treatment groups, complete follow-up, and inclusion of 149 cases in final analysis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a horizontal dot plot showing isolate counts for bacteria, with Staphylococcus aureus highest at 48, followed by other bacterial isolates at 21, Escherichia coli at 11, Klebsiella pneumoniae at 8, and Viridans streptococci at 7. Panel B features a violin plot comparing pretreatment Cobb angles between confirmed and not confirmed groups, displaying similar distributions and medians. Panel C displays a vertical bar chart of positive rates with group A at 82.4 percent, group B at 84.2 percent, and group C at 40.0 percent.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Panel with four line graphs compares outcomes across three groups \(A in blue, B in yellow, C in red\). Graph \(A\) shows CRP \(mg/L\), \(B\) ESR \(mm/h\), \(C\) VAS \(pain scale\), and \(D\) ODI \(disability index\), each measured at baseline, 1 month, 3 months, 6 months, and final. All graphs show downward trends, with Groups B and C demonstrating greater reductions over time compared to Group A. Individual patient trajectories are indicated by thin lines and group means by thicker highlighted lines with points.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Four grouped violin plots compare three groups, labeled A, B, and C, on four different medical outcomes: \(A\) shows C-reactive protein \(CRP\) reduction at one month, \(B\) shows erythrocyte sedimentation rate \(ESR\) reduction at three months, \(C\) shows Oswestry Disability Index \(ODI\) improvement at final follow-up, and \(D\) shows Cobb correction in final degrees. Each plot displays distribution, median, and interquartile range. Statistically significant differences between groups, marked by asterisks, are indicated with connecting lines above the plots.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Multipanel spinal imaging figure showing representative radiographs, computed tomography, magnetic resonance imaging, and three-dimensional reconstructions from a patient with pyogenic spondylitis. The images demonstrate infection-related vertebral and intervertebral structural abnormalities, spinal alignment and Cobb angle measurements, and radiological changes across imaging modalities.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Panel of spinal medical images showing radiographs, CT scans, MRI scans, and histology at various stages of spinal pathology and surgical intervention. Images include annotated spinal alignment measurements, fixation hardware, 3D reconstructions, axial and sagittal slices, and histological detail in the final panel.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Radiographic, CT, 3D reconstruction, and MRI images arranged in labeled panels A through R display the thoracolumbar spine before and after surgical intervention; multiple images show hardware placement, spinal alignment correction, cross-sectional anatomy, sagittal and axial views, Cobb angle measurements, and a microscopic pathology slide.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Figure with three grouped dot plot panels illustrating adjusted differences between groups B vs A and C vs A. Panel A displays percentage point differences for CRP reduction at one month, ESR reduction at three months, and final ODI improvement. Panel B shows adjusted degree difference for final Cobb correction. Panel C depicts point difference for VAS reduction at one month. Dots represent means; horizontal lines indicate confidence intervals, with yellow for B vs A and red for C vs A. All axes labeled, with group and outcome identifiers included.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
